  'Every year, about one third of all the food produced in the world is lost or thrown away.', 'This means that while millions of people go hungry, a huge amount of food ends up in the garbage.',
  'Food waste happens at every stage, from the farm to the kitchen table.', 'On farms, vegetables that do not look perfect are often left in the fields because stores refuse to buy them.',
  'In supermarkets, food is removed from the shelves as soon as it reaches its best-before date, even though it is still safe to eat.',
  'At home, many people buy more than they need and forget about the food in the back of their refrigerators.', 'Throwing away food is not only a waste of money but also harmful to the environment.',
  'When food rots in landfills, it produces methane, a gas that contributes to global warming.', 'Moreover, the water and energy used to grow and transport the food are wasted as well.',
  'Some countries have started to take action against this problem.', 'In France, for example, large supermarkets are required by law to donate unsold food to charities.',
  'In Japan, some restaurants now let customers take their leftovers home in special boxes.',
  'Individuals can also make a difference by planning their meals and buying only what they will actually eat.', 'Small changes in our daily habits, if many people make them, can have a big impact.',
